WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.651
In this video, you will bring in help.

00:00:02.651 --> 00:00:08.654
You will add co-organizers, who share the work of running the contest, and judges, who score the homes.

00:00:08.654 --> 00:00:09.808
We start on the map.

00:00:10.714 --> 00:00:14.776
To begin, open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:14.776 --> 00:00:16.901
That is the only address you need.

00:00:18.736 --> 00:00:21.143
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:21.143 --> 00:00:24.887
The first time you visit, it asks to use your location.

00:00:24.887 --> 00:00:26.224
Tap Use my location.

00:00:28.002 --> 00:00:32.439
That is how the map shows how far things are, and gives you directions.

00:00:32.439 --> 00:00:35.644
Your browser asks permission as well, so tap Allow.

00:00:35.644 --> 00:00:40.204
Your location is used only on your device, and you can say no at any time.

00:00:43.828 --> 00:00:46.517
Now look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:46.517 --> 00:00:47.712
See the three dots?

00:00:47.712 --> 00:00:52.015
That is the menu, and it is the doorway to everything else on the site.

00:00:52.015 --> 00:00:52.553
Tap them.

00:00:54.162 --> 00:00:55.800
In the menu, tap Contests.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:01:01.138
That is where every neighborhood contest lives: the ones you can vote in, enter, or run.

00:01:02.847 --> 00:01:03.430
Tap Mine.

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:05.061
This is your personal page.

00:01:05.061 --> 00:01:10.420
It lists the contests you run, if you run any, and the homes you entered, with their status.

00:01:12.101 --> 00:01:14.147
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:01:14.147 --> 00:01:17.818
This opens your dashboard, the control room for your contest.

00:01:19.724 --> 00:01:22.160
Running a contest is easier with help.

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:22.784
Tap Team.

00:01:22.784 --> 00:01:30.092
Co-organizers get the same dashboard you have, so they can approve entries, answer questions, and keep things moving.

00:01:31.934 --> 00:01:35.134
Type their email address, and tap Add co-organizer.

00:01:38.692 --> 00:01:42.971
They get an email like this one, with one button that opens the dashboard.

00:01:42.971 --> 00:01:46.052
They sign in with that email address, and they are in.

00:01:47.058 --> 00:01:49.622
Judges are different from co-organizers.

00:01:49.622 --> 00:01:53.250
They score the homes, but they do not manage the contest.

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:56.252
They are added on the Judges tab, so tap Judges.

00:01:58.039 --> 00:02:00.930
Type a judge's email address, and tap Add judge.

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:07.361
You can see who has signed in, and how many homes each judge has scored, so you know the judging is on track.

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:12.218
Your judge gets an invitation like this one.

00:02:12.218 --> 00:02:18.376
It says which contest it is, how judging works, and has a button that opens their private ballot.

00:02:18.376 --> 00:02:19.822
Nothing else to set up.

00:02:20.829 --> 00:02:22.471
Next up: Announce winners.
